 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the New York state medical care facilities finance agency act, in relation to the ability to issue certain bonds and notes",
    "basePrintNo": "S4200",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4200-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §7, NYS Med Care Fac Fin Ag Act",
    "lawSection": "New York State Medical Care Facilities Finance Agency Act",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4200\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act\nto amend the New York state medical care facilities finance agency act,\nin relation to the ability to issue certain bonds and notes\n\nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would increase the authorization of the New York State\nDormitory Authority (\"Authority\" or \"Dormitory Authority\"), as\nsuccessor to the New York State Medical Care Facilities Finance\nAgency (\"MCFFA\") pursuant to the Health Care Financing Consolidation\nAct of 1995, to issue hospital and nursing home project bonds and\nnotes from $15 billion to $15.8 billion dollars.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill would amend the MCFFA Act to increase the\nAuthority's authorization to issue hospital and nursing home project\nbonds and notes from $15 billion to $15.8 billion dollars.\n\nSection two of the bill sets forth the effective date.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nParagraph (b) of subdivision 1 of section 7 of section 1 of Chapter\n392 of the Laws of 1973, constituting the New York State Medical Care\nFacilities Finance Agency Act, as last amended by Chapter 238 of the\nLaws of 2009, provides that that the Authority shall not issue\nhospital and nursing home project bonds and notes in an aggregate\nprincipal amount exceeding $15 billion dollars.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\nSTATEMENT IN SUPPORT:\n\nThe Dormitory Authority issues bonds for the purpose of funding\nmortgage loans or project loans to not-for-profit hospital and\nnursing home corporations. Some of the bonds issued for the\nAuthority's hospital and nursing home clients are issued under the\nMCFFA Act's federally aided mortgage loan program, which involves\nobtaining Federal Housing Administration (\"FHA\") mortgage insurance.\n\nBonds issued pursuant to both of these programs are subject to the\ncurrent hospital and nursing home project bond authorization cap in\nthe MCFFA Act of $15 billion. This authorization was most recently\nincreased by $800,000,000 in 2009.\n\nAs of January 10, 2011, the Dormitory Authority has sold and closed\nbond transactions in the amount of $622,500,000. Thus, $644,934,493\nof capacity under the existing statutory limitation is available for\nother transactions. There are, however, currently four hospital and\n\n\nnursing home financings in the Authority's current \"pipeline\"\ntotaling about $315,000,000. This bill is necessary to ensure that\nthe Authority has sufficient capacity to support additional projects\nas they seek financing.\n\nAlthough the Authority cannot predict exactly when these proposed\nfinancings will actually occur, the Authority is seeking additional\nbond authorization at this time to ensure that it will be able to\nmeet the needs of all its private not-for-profit health-care clients\non a timely basis. Absent the timely enactment of this legislation,\nsome hospital and nursing homes would be required to defer projects\nthat are necessary to enable these institutions to meet the health\ncare needs of those they serve.\n\nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThere are no budget implications from this bill.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThe bill would take effect immediately upon enactment.\n\n",
